omeone inside the walls if you  can't  we're doomed to repeat it all again the  same history the same mistakes  again and again if you want to save them  all mikasa armin  and the others carry out your mission to  the end  end quote this conversation between  krueger and grisha could also be a way  for future aaron to give a message to  the past aaron who is currently  witnessing grisha's memories  in this way aaron is telling himself to  carry out his mission to the end  to not stop until he breaks the loop and  although you could say that when kruger  says doomed to repeat it all again  he just means that future generations  will keep the cycle of hatred going when  you take everything else into account  it's hard not to believe that he's  talking about repeating it all again  because of the time loop you can find  more and more instances like this  littered throughout the story that can  easily be read as having something to do  with the time loop or referring to the  time loop  during chapter 6 before mikisa saves  aaron from a kidnapper she mentions that  she remembers and i quote  seeing this scene before again and again  end quote  as with the kruger moment you can  explain it away by saying that she was  just referring to the world being a  cruel place  and how the strong feet on the weak  she's seen those laws in nature at work  before  and i do think she meant that however at  the same time i also think that this  could be pointing to the fact that they  are  in a time loop repeating things over and  over again consciously mikasa would not  recall past  lives at this point except maybe through  a deja vu experience  but i do think ackerman's have a higher  chance of getting access to memories  of past loops than the other ldns  because their memories are more  difficult to manipulate  than that of the others in fact so far  it's been suggested that their memories  can't actually be rewritten like that of  the other aldeans  using the founding titan power you may  have noticed that the ackermans get  headaches a lot  it is possible that they get headaches  because memories of past  time loops are coming to them while  their mind resists them  notably mikasa's latest headache leads  to her vision of the cabin house which  we're saying for the sake of this video  is what happened in the previous time  loop once she says  she can't take this anymore as if she  can't hold the memory at bay anymore  she gets this vision and she no longer  has a headache  we know that aaron or amir shouldn't be  able to feed  any false memories to an ackerman so  this it would seem  must be a real memory a real memory of a  past life  let's keep going with how other things  can be viewed differently through the  lens of this theory the attack titan's  ability to see future memories might  actually be the ability to see the  memories of  past time loops thus a future memory  could just be a memory of a past  loop that was further along than the  present loop the attack  titan that is always moving forward and  seeking freedom from the loop  might be the only titan power that when  combined with the founding titan power  can gain  full access to the memories of all past  loops  in turn this would explain why aaron is  acting the way he is now  and why he's doing such horrible things  because he may be aware that he tried  every other alternative in every past  loop and it failed to break the cycle  so now this is the only alternative left  he had to be mean  and distant to mikasa and armin where  things may never have worked out the way  they did  so this brings us back to the latest  chapter chapter 138 where aaron seems to  have finally broken the time loop by  having mikasa kill him  the current founding titan while the  shiny centipede creature was outside of  its host's body  in the last panel we saw emir fritz in  the back smiling  suggesting that aaron completed the goal  he promised he would  if she lent him her power he put an end  to it to the loop once and for all  now the shiny centipede creature's cord  to the aldians has been cut  and in the next chapter aldians should  end up being freed from the curse of the  titans in other words  they'll be like everyone else they won't  be able to turn into titans anymore  they won't be affected by amir's curse  the world of paths will cease to exist  and emir and aaron will finally be able  to rest in peace  if you don't know islam has already  revealed what the final panel of the  manga will be  it will be a baby probably historia's  baby being held by an  adult and they will tell the baby and i  quote you are  free my interpretation of this is that  the baby will be free of the titan curse  thanks to aaron  not only has the rest of the world seen  aldians risking their lives to stop  aaron the devil  if aldians will also cease to be able to  become titans once and for all  as i expect then the surviving  inhabitants of the world  will really have no reason to treat the  remaining aliens like monsters and  discriminate against them  thus this aldean baby will also be free  of the world's fear and hatred that all  past aldians were  subject to armin and the others will  stop being able to turn into titans and  they will also be free from emir's curse  just as kruger told grisha aaron will  have carried out his mission to the end  and in that way he will have saved  mikasa and armin  and the aldian nation as a whole just as  he wanted to do  all along and that my friends will be  the end of attack on titan one of the  greatest stories  ever told now before i wrap up i just  want to address some other facets of the  theory  one of the main questions is how is a  time loop possible  well just as in haruhi suzumiya it's  possible that a godlike character is  responsible while the haruki suzumiya  time loop was caused by haruhi who has  the godlike abilities to change destroy  and reshape reality in that series  it is possible the attack on titan time  loop was caused by amir fritz who  similarly has  the godlike abilities to change destroy  and reshape reality in her own series if  amir who once possessed all nine titan  powers  can transcend time and space as we've  seen it's not that far fetched to assume  that she could create a time loop that  would repeat  until someone like aaron helped her  achieve her desired outcome of freedom  while researching the endless 8 i also  came across  something which i thought was  interesting some fans suggested that  they made  the endless 8 arc last 8 episodes  because  8 the number looks like the sign  infinity infinity in turn points to the  idea of being in an infinite time loop  the concluding episode of the endless 8  arc where the infinity loop was broken  was the 19th episode broadcast for  season 2  or the 9th new episode either way the  interesting thing is that the number  nine physically looks like the number  eight or the infinity sign would look  if the loop was broken so it's very  fitting that the endless eight loop was  broken on the ninth episode i am fully  aware  that i may be looking too much into this  but i like to look at numbers especially  when we're talking about time travel  in attack on time's case it seems random  to finish on the 139th  chapter however since that will be the  first chapter where the characters have  actually escaped the time loop and are  finally free from it  it seems very fitting for it to end with  a 9  just like with haruhi suzumiya and the  number 13 in front of the 9  is not insignificant either as we know  13 represents emir's curse in attack on  titan and by extension  the titan curse more generally while the  numbers 13  8 suggests that we are trapped in a  cursed and endless titan time loop  13 9 suggests that we finally escaped  the cursed  titan time loop and emir's curse again  this last part  may be looking into it way too much and  i fully acknowledge that but i thought  it was interesting nonetheless and so i  wanted to share it in light of  everything else we know  about the time loop trope and the attack  on titan series  anyways that is it for this video thank  you so much for watching  let me know whether you think the time  loop theory will pan out for attack on  titan or not  either way i hope you enjoyed the video  no matter what happens i personally  enjoy this theory  so much that i will consider it an  alternate ending if isayama doesn't  actually end up using it  if you did enjoy this video and want to  keep the attack on titan videos coming  then the best thing you could do  is warhammer smash that like button  until it's blue  imagine this what if we're in a time  loop right now  and the only way out is for you to  finally smash that like button  our collective fate is in your hands if  you haven't be sure to subscribe  and hit that notification bell and  select all or you will miss future  attack on titan videos  and while you wait for the next one to  drop feel free to check out our growing  attack on time playlist where i got  videos about all the time shifters all  the acronyms and much more  link to that is in the description also  feel free to leave suggestions for  future attack on time videos  that you are burning up to see in the  comments and until next time  see ya space cowboys  [Music]  you
 

